      "summary": "Guest preacher Pastor Chad Vendix Horn (OPC, Philadelphia Presbytery) preaches on Acts 8:26-40 — the encounter between Philip and the Ethiopian eunuch on the desert road to Gaza. The sermon traces God's sovereign preparation of the encounter through five providential arrangements, Philip's obedient response without explanation (like Abraham), the theological significance of the Ethiopian's situation (a eunuch excluded from the temple assembly, reading Isaiah 53 about a suffering Servant who bears exclusion and shame), Philip's preaching of Christ from Isaiah 53, and the Ethiopian's baptism and joy. The Reformation insight about two religions — managing sin versus confessing it and looking to a Substitute — anchors the application.",
