            "1 John 5:1 in the original Greek: 'Whoever believes that Jesus is the Christ has been born [perfect tense — completed prior action] of God' — the perfect tense (has been born) grammatically precedes the present tense (believes); the birth comes before the believing",
            "We are completely passive in regeneration: Ephesians 2:5 — 'even when we were dead in trespasses, [God] made us alive together with Christ' — the dead don't contribute to being made alive",
            "Psalm 119:32 (NIV): 'I run in the path of your commands, for you have set my heart free' — the running (faith and obedience) follows the heart's liberation by God",
