      "summary": "Continuing the series on the first year of Jesus' public ministry, Pastor Tito Lyro preaches on John 3:16-21, focusing on verse 16 in the morning. The sermon examines what is perhaps the best-known and most misunderstood verse in the Bible. The 'so' (houtōs) describes *how* God loved — in this manner — not the intensity; a colon better captures it: 'God loved the world in this manner: he gave his Son.' The object of that love, 'the world,' refers in John to all kinds of people, as confirmed by Revelation 7:9-10. Three significant sections develop God's love: (1) the Trinitarian dimension — the same love with which the Father loves the Son (John 3:35; 15:9; 17:23-26) is the love extended to the believer; the Spirit pours this love into our hearts (Romans 5:5); (2) the undeserved nature — God loved us while we were helpless, ungodly, sinners, and enemies (Romans 5:6-10; Romans 1 is our spiritual biography); (3) the gift — 'only begotten' (monogenēs) means unique; Romans 8:32 proves the lesser from the greater. Saving faith is defined as knowledge, assent, and trust — all three together. Eternal life is not merely future but is experienced now in the Word, the Spirit's communion, the Lord's Supper, and the fellowship of the church.",
