            "Father died when Robinson was eight; sent to London as an indentured barber's apprentice",
            "Fell in with a gang; got a gypsy drunk to tell his fortune — was told he'd have a long life, a wife, and children",
            "Went to disrupt George Whitefield's preaching; became transfixed instead",
            "Whitefield preached from Matthew 3:7 ('flee from the wrath to come')",
            "The sermon haunted Robinson for two years before he trusted Christ in 1752",
            "Illustration of a Puritan who heard a sermon at age 17 and was converted at age 92"
