            "Passed through a small, poor Baptist congregation; supplemented income by farming and speaking",
            "Wrote several books on Baptist history; became the foremost Baptist scholar of his age",
            "Raised twelve children; died at age 54, likely from overwork",
            "Falsely rumored to have abandoned the faith; solidly Trinitarian sermons survive from the end of his life",
            "Short autobiographical note in Latin: 'Reborn 24 May 1752 by the power of the preaching of George Whitefield'"
