      "outline": [
        {
          "title": "Introduction: The Seven I AM Statements of Jesus in John",
          "subpoints": [
            "The seven I AM statements (John 6, 8, 10, 11, 14, 15) are titles and metaphors for how Jesus relates to His covenantal people",
            "In addition, John 8 contains three (or four) I AM statements where Jesus declares His deity directly",
            "Context: Feast of Tabernacles, temple courts — Jewish leadership increasingly hostile"
          ],
          "scripture": [
            "John 8:12-59"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "1. I Am the Light of the World (John 8:12)",
          "subpoints": [
            "Setting: court of women at the Feast of Tabernacles, where large lamps were lit each night and men danced with torches",
            "OT allusions: pillar of fire (Exod. 13-14), Word as lamp (Ps. 119:105), Isaiah 49:6 (Messianic servant as light to the Gentiles), Isaiah 60:19-20 (Yahweh as everlasting light)",
            "The Pharisees objected: His testimony is that of only one witness — they missed the deeper claim",
            "Light is its own witness — it testifies simply by shining",
            "Jesus's divine testimony is sufficient — He is from above; they are from below"
          ],
          "scripture": [
            "John 8:12",
            "Isaiah 49:6",
            "Isaiah 60:19-20"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "2. I Am the Testifying One (John 8:18) — The Subtle Fifth I AM",
          "subpoints": [
            "In asserting 'I am the one who testifies about Myself,' Jesus declares His own divine witness",
            "He has two witnesses: Himself and the Father — greater than the two required by the law",
            "The Pharisees did not know who Jesus was, or who His Father was — without accepting the divine revelation of Jesus, one cannot know the Father"
          ],
          "scripture": [
            "John 8:18"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "3. Without Belief That Jesus Is Yahweh, You Will Die in Your Sins (John 8:24)",
          "subpoints": [
            "'For if you do not believe that I am, you will die in your sins' — no predicate follows 'I am'",
            "In Hebrew/Aramaic, Jesus likely said 'ehyeh' — the Exodus 3:14 self-designation of Yahweh",
            "Isaiah 43:10-11: 'You are My witnesses... that you may know and believe Me and understand that I am. Before Me there was no God formed, nor shall there be after Me'",
            "The Jews heard Jesus say 'I am' with no predicate and demanded: 'I am — what? Who are you?' — willful ignorance (Isaiah 6:9-10)"
          ],
          "scripture": [
            "John 8:24",
            "Exodus 3:14",
            "Isaiah 43:10-11"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "4. The Crucifixion Will Validate the Deity of Jesus (John 8:28)",
          "subpoints": [
            "'When you lift up the Son of Man, then you will know that I am' — no predicate",
            "Three assertions: (1) He is the Son of Man (deity and humanity, from Daniel 7); (2) He does only what the Father commands; (3) He is I AM",
            "The Heidelberg Catechism: our Mediator must be true man (to pay what man owes) and true God (to bear the full weight of God's wrath in His humanity)",
            "God the Father validated Christ's acceptable work by raising Him from the dead",
            "Many appeared to believe (v.30) but subsequent dialogue reveals false, shallow faith"
          ],
          "scripture": [
            "John 8:28",
            "Daniel 7"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "5. Jesus Is the Eternal God, Yahweh (John 8:58)",
          "subpoints": [
            "'Before Abraham was, I am' — not 'I was' but 'I am' — asserting eternal, timeless existence",
            "At this the Jews took up stones: they now understood exactly what He was claiming",
            "This is the climactic declaration of the entire chapter — and the Jews' response proved they understood it as a claim to deity"
          ],
          "scripture": [
            "John 8:58"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Application",
          "subpoints": [
            "The question is: how will you respond to Jesus's claims?",
            "He is Yahweh; there is no other God beside Him; there is salvation in no other",
            "He lived the life we could not live; He died the death we could not die — believe in Him and walk in His light"
          ],
          "scripture": []
        }
      ],
      "summary": "Elder Scott Hollander preaches through the four I AM statements of Jesus in John 8 (plus a subtle fifth), demonstrating that Jesus is explicitly claiming to be Yahweh — the eternal self-existent God of the Old Testament. Moving from 'I am the light of the world' (v.12) through the absolute I AM declarations (vv.24, 28, 58), he establishes each claim against its Old Testament background, paying particular attention to the Greek and Hebrew of Exodus 3 and Isaiah 43, and to the Heidelberg Catechism's articulation of why the Mediator must be both truly man and truly God. The climax is John 8:58 — 'Before Abraham was, I am' — which caused the Jews to take up stones immediately.",
      "soundcloud_url": "https://soundcloud.com/olympiabp/02-11-24-am-jesus-is-the-i-am-john-8_12-30-elder-scott-hollander"
