      "summary": "Guest preacher Pastor H. Dennis Leaman (former pastor of the congregation) preaches on Psalm 51 — David's prayer of repentance after Nathan confronted him about his sin with Bathsheba and the murder of Uriah. The sermon distinguishes attrition (sorrow at being caught) from contrition (genuine godly sorrow), and draws four observations from David's prayer: David's year of silence produced physical and spiritual deterioration (Psalm 32); sin is ultimately against God, which is why repentance must be vertical; true repentance is specific and thorough, asking not to feel better but to be genuinely cleansed; and the restoration of assurance follows genuine repentance — a broken and contrite heart God will not despise. A call to preach repentance as essential to genuine conversion closes the sermon.",
