      "summary": "Continuing the 1 Peter series, Pastor Tito Lyro focuses on verse 18 — 'For Christ also suffered once for sins, the just for the unjust, that He might bring us to God.' Five aspects of Christ's saving work are examined: (1) his identity as the Messiah, the Righteous One, Yahweh Our Righteousness; (2) those he saves — the unrighteous, described in Romans 3:9-18 as totally depraved, in active rebellion against God; (3) his substitutionary work — the singular righteous for the plural unjust, dying for what he did not deserve; (4) the result — bringing sinners to God; (5) the efficacy — once for all, nothing to add. A strong application challenges the pride hidden in self-punishment after forgiveness, urging believers to be satisfied with the complete work of Christ.",
