      "summary": "In this Sunday evening sermon on 1 Peter 3:22, preached on Ascension Sunday, Pastor Tito Lyro explores the doctrine of the session of Christ — Jesus's ongoing ministry as He is enthroned and ruling at the right hand of the Father in heaven. He explains why this terminology is used in church government: when elders are seated together in governance they are \"in session,\" and when Christ is seated on the throne He is ruling all creation for the church. The work of Christ did not end with the resurrection; it continued through the ascension and the session, and it continues now.\n\nWorking through 1 Peter 3:22 carefully, Pastor Lyro explains that the right hand is a position of both authority and execution — like Joseph at Pharaoh's right hand or Mordecai at the king's right hand. Prior to this position of session, angels, authorities, and powers were subjected to Christ — a subjection accomplished at the cross and confirmed at the resurrection. The ascension is therefore a coronation parade in which the conquering king displays his victory and distributes gifts to his people, specifically the teaching offices of the church (Ephesians 4:11-12). By virtue of union with Christ, believers have ascended with Him and now dwell positionally in the heavenly places — which is the basis for Christian ethics.\n\nIn His session, Christ is actively pouring out the Holy Spirit, forgiving the sins of His people, interceding for them before the Father, and working to preserve them to the end. This results in three practical applications: believers are equipped to conduct spiritual warfare under Christ's authority, are free from the fear of demonic powers, and are empowered to make disciples of all nations through the Great Commission — because all authority in heaven and earth belongs to the One who is their Head."
