      "summary": "Preaching for the first time in 25 years of ministry from the book of Numbers, Pastor Lyro delivers the Aaronic benediction (Numbers 6:22-27) as a farewell message for the Hoy family, who are leaving to serve the Lord with a church plant in Australia. He establishes that while Aaron and his priestly sons speak the words, it is God himself who blesses — the three-fold repetition of the divine name Yahweh in verses 24-26 making unmistakably clear that the source of every blessing is the Lord. The sermon draws out that the Aaronic benediction became the template for Paul's apostolic greetings and that God explicitly commands the priest, amid all his duties, to remind the people of God's blessing upon them. The three strophes of the benediction are unpacked — God's protecting keeping, his gracious shining face, and his gift of peace — with the note that God never blesses meagerly: 2 Corinthians 9:8 describes a grace that is all-sufficient for every good work. The congregation is called to recognize that the presence of God in their lives — growth in holiness, deepening hatred of sin — is itself the greatest blessing, and that the Hoys depart not on the basis of the church's commendation alone but bearing the very name of the Lord."
