      "summary": "In the second lesson of the adult Sunday School series on the Ministry of the Holy Spirit, Pastor Tito Lyro establishes from Scripture that the Holy Spirit is fully God — not an impersonal force or a lesser being — through four lines of argument: divine names and titles (OT passages attributed to Yahweh are quoted in the NT as words of the Spirit), divine attributes (omniscience, omnipresence, omnipotence), divine works (creation, miracles, regeneration), and divine worship (the apostolic benediction, baptism, the blasphemy passage). He then examines the offices within the Trinity, distinguishing between the ontological Trinity and the economic Trinity, and explains that the Father is the source of all things, the Son is the agent, and the Spirit is the means by which the Godhead accomplishes its will. The Spirit eternally proceeds from the Father and the Son (the filioque), and while the persons are subordinate in office they are equal in being. The lesson closes with the first thirteen of thirty-eight ways the Spirit ministers to creation and the church, beginning with the Spirit causing the new birth and culminating in the Spirit testifying of Christ and inspiring Scripture."
