            "Leopold's description: an 'overstrained righteousness' that loses sight of our sinful imperfections and argues with God for not rewarding us as we think we deserve",
            "The right path is not a mediocre middle road, but God-fearing faithfulness that is humble before Him",
            "'Fear God' (v. 18) is reverential trust and awe that causes us to want to please and honor God",
            "The conclusion of the whole book (Eccl. 12:13): 'Fear God and keep His commandments' — this section points toward that summary"
