      "summary": "Guest preacher Pastor Kevin Backus expounds Ecclesiastes 7:13–18, drawing extensively on Thomas Boston's 'The Crook in the Lot.' The sermon argues that while fatalism sees an impersonal force ordaining the difficulties of life, the Bible's teaching is that a personal, loving, all-knowing God sovereignly ordains the 'lot' — the pathway — for every believer, including its 'crooks': those painful circumstances that run cross-purposes to what we would have chosen. The proper response is to consider God's work, receive both prosperity and adversity as from His hand, avoid self-righteous demands on God, and fear Him in reverential trust — the summary of Ecclesiastes as a whole.",
