      "summary": "Guest speaker Pastor Chris Lensch traces the identity of Jesus as God's Lamb from John the Baptist's proclamation in John 1 through the heavenly visions of Revelation. Beginning with John's declaration 'Behold the Lamb of God who takes away the sin of the world,' he shows that Jesus is uniquely qualified as both perfect man and eternal Son of God to serve as the final high priest who offers himself as the atoning sacrifice. The sermon weaves together the Lamb's humility in his first coming with his exaltation as the one worthy to open the scroll of judgment.\n\nDrawing from Revelation 5, 6, and 19, Lensch presents the full arc of the Lamb's story: from humble sacrifice to wrathful judge and joyful bridegroom. Those who spurn God's Lamb will face his wrath at history's end, while those invited to the marriage supper of the Lamb will reign with him forever. The sermon closes with the encouragement that the risen Lamb intercedes for his people now and will receive them to himself at his return."
