      "summary": "In this Sunday School lecture, Dr. John Battle of Western Reformed Seminary demonstrates that Alexander the Great's rapid conquests (ca. 336-323 BC) were precise fulfillments of prophecies written over 200 years earlier in Ezekiel and Daniel. From the literal scraping of Tyre to the four-horned division of his empire, every major prophetic detail was fulfilled exactly, confirming that God governs the rise and fall of nations for his own purposes.\n\nBeyond fulfilled prophecy, Dr. Battle shows how God used Alexander to prepare the ancient world for the gospel. By spreading Hellenistic Greek throughout the Middle East, North Africa, and Central Asia, Alexander unknowingly created the linguistic infrastructure through which the New Testament would be written and the apostles would preach. The most unknown Christian is more precious in God's sight than the greatest conqueror—yet God uses even conquerors to build his church."
