      "summary": "Preaching from 1 John 2:18-27, Pastor Tito Lyro takes up John's confrontation with the antichrists — teachers who had been in the visible church and who claimed to possess special knowledge unavailable to ordinary believers, while denying that Jesus was fully man and fully God. The sermon presents two closely related points: those truly born from above will not be deceived by such false teaching, and the Holy Spirit and the Word of God together preserve the believer in commitment to the Christ of the Bible.\n\nThe antichrists' departure from the church exposed their true nature — they had never been united to Christ, however long they sat in the pews or however effectively they seemed to minister. John's use of the same word for their going out as he used of Judas leaving the upper room is deliberate and chilling. By contrast, those who are truly the Father's have been given to the Son, and the Son will lose none of them (John 6:37-40). The anointing every believer has received — the indwelling Holy Spirit — is the Spirit who leads to the real Jesus and who, working inseparably with the apostolic Word (the Scriptures), guards against every distortion of Christ.\n\nThe sermon presses toward a practical test: the first and most essential question about any teacher is whether he gets Christ right — fully man, fully God, the only Savior. The sermon closes with a personal and searching call: do you believe in this Jesus — the Christ of the Bible — right now? That belief is the difference between eternal life with God and eternal life under his wrath."
