      "summary": "Pastor Tito Lyro opens the Gimmel stanza of Psalm 119 (vv. 17-24) with a focus on verse 18's prayer 'Open my eyes that I may see wonderful things from your law.' The sermon establishes two rails of Bible reading that carry the soul toward holiness: prayer before God's throne and meditation on his Word. Using the structure of Psalm 119 itself, he identifies four realities about spiritual sight—that there are wonderful things in the Word, that we cannot see them without God's supernatural help, that seeing them transforms us into Christ's image, and that they are found supremely in Christ himself.\n\nThe heart of the sermon is a survey of seven types of prayer drawn from all 176 verses of Psalm 119, each one showing how our Bible reading must be saturated with dependence on God to teach, not hide, illuminate, incline our hearts toward, give life for, establish our steps by, and pursue us back to his Word. Pastor Lyro closes by challenging the congregation to pray and study together—not choosing between them—ransacking the Scriptures like prospectors seeking gold and like a bride hunting for a lost ring."
