      "summary": "Expounding 1 John 2:15-17, Pastor Tito Lyro addresses the tension every Christian lives in: the already-not-yet space between what Christ has accomplished and his return to make all things new. He carefully defines what the 'world' means in this passage—not the physical creation or lost humanity as a whole, but the kingdom of darkness whose ruler and inhabitants are in rebellion against God—and shows why love for this world is incompatible with love for the Father.\n\nThe sermon distinguishes between false ways of overcoming worldliness (isolation, cultural power, withdrawal) and the genuine biblical approach: deciding to fight, owning your identity in Christ, practicing contentment, and living a life of self-denial produced by grace. Practical and honest throughout, Pastor Lyro even names television as his personal idol, modeling the transparency he calls for in the congregation. The sermon closes with four summary ways to overcome: believing in Christ as Son of God, purifying the heart, living to please God, and living for the eternal world to come."
