      "summary": "Preaching the magnificent benediction of Hebrews 13:20-25, Pastor Tito Lyro traces three movements: who God is, what God does, and how we respond. God is 'the God of the peace'—not a general peacefulness but the very wholeness and satisfaction the human heart craves, found only in him through the Lord Jesus Christ. He established this peace by raising Jesus from the dead through the blood of the everlasting covenant, proving the Father received the Son's sacrifice on behalf of his people.\n\nThe sermon turns on the beautiful description of Jesus as 'that great shepherd of the sheep,' exploring how helpless sheep are without a shepherd and how tenderly Christ leads, gathers, and provides. Because of who God is and what he has done, his people are equipped with every good thing they need to do his will—through his Word, his Spirit, his undershepherds, and his people. The sermon closes with a doxological application: when we run from the means of grace, we run from peace itself; and when we behold who God is and what he has done, we cannot help but break into praise."
