      "summary": "Preached on the occasion of the nation's 245th Independence Day, Pastor Tito Lyro expounds Proverbs 14:33 through 15:2 to examine God's relationship to nations and to diagnose the spiritual condition of the United States. He begins by establishing the absolute sovereignty of God over all nations without exception — they are tools in His hands, and their rebellion never frustrates His purposes. God has revealed in His word what He desires for nations: that they follow His moral law, particularly the second table of the Ten Commandments, and that they treat His people with justice and kindness.\n\nPastor Lyro then assesses where the United States stands in the spectrum of righteousness and shame described in Proverbs 14:34. He acknowledges the nation's Christian founding — the warp and woof of its founding documents assumed a moral and religious people — but does not flinch from declaring that America has fallen drastically from that foundation. Abortion, the sexual revolution, the worship of creation, and the imposition of anti-biblical ideologies are all cited as evidence that the nation is calling evil good and good evil. The sermon ends not with despair but with a call to the church: as goes the church, so goes the nation. The only path forward is for the church to return to her single mission — discipling the nations through the faithful preaching of God's Word and the equipping of God's people — trusting that the Holy Spirit will use the proclaimed word to raise up a great army for the Lord, as in Ezekiel 37."
